{"title": "Samsung’s paid Galaxy AI plan has a giant Gemini problem", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/10/samsungs-paid-ai-ambitions-have-a-giant-gemini-problem/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/03/galaxy-s26-series-ai-4.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Good morning. Today I’m trying desperately not to buy <a href=\"https://howl.link/link/?url=https%3A%2F%2Felectronics.sony.com%2Faudio%2Fheadphones%2Fheadband%2Fp%2Fmdr3r-s&publisher_slug=9to5&article_name=Affiliate+Link+Tool&article_url=https%3A%2F%2F9to5mac.com&u1=danielbader\">Sony’s new nostalgia-bait headphones</a>, reeling from how emotionally invested I was in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider-Man:_Brand_New_Day\">Spider-Man: Brand New Day</a> (yes, I know I’m late), trying to figure out what a “<a href=\"https://medium.com/blog/tk-a-new-private-notebook-app-from-medium-13d3d6efdce1\">private, agentic notebook</a>” is, and slowly coming around to the idea of the <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/05/business/media/letterboxd-new-york-times-company.html\">New York Times owning Letterboxd</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Inbox</em> is the tech newsletter that goes beyond the news cycle. We cover the most important 9to5Google stories from the last couple of days along with a few highlights from around the web. We publish every Tuesday and Thursday, and if you like what you read, <a href=\"https://9to5google.beehiiv.com/subscribe\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">please subscribe</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/10/samsungs-paid-ai-ambitions-have-a-giant-gemini-problem/#more-736299\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-10T03:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-10T17:38:42.816641+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
