{"title": "Pixelated 124: Is it time for a Nest Hub comeback?", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/06/pixelated-124-is-it-time-for-a-nest-hub-comeback/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2024/03/Pixelated-cover.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Welcome to Pixelated episode 124. This week, Damien, Abner, and Will dive into the announcement of Motorola’s flagship return in North America, the Signature 27. Is a $1,600 non-foldable the comeback everyone hoped for, or is this device doomed by rising component costs? Then, with Apple’s HomeView smart display set to launch next week, the gang examines Google’s lack of a modernized competitor and wonder what they’d want to see from a relaunch in 2027.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Enjoy the show? You can listen to our weekly members-only Pixelated Pro bonus episode by <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/pro/\">signing up for 9to5Google Pro</a> for just $5 per month, or about $1 per episode.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Sponsored by Proton Unlimited</strong>: Pixelated listeners can save 30% on an annual subscription to the company’s suite of privacy-friendly services by <a href=\"https://proton.me/9to5google\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">signing up using our link</a>. Thanks to Proton Unlimited for sponsoring the podcast.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio controls=\"controls\" src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/pix-124.mp3\"></audio></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-subscribe\">Subscribe</h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLcKP282Ii48tKK_KUt1kq1Ist9FkYR6lO\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">YouTube Podcasts</a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://pca.st/podcast/ac8e6ce0-06b1-0136-c264-7d73a919276a\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" targ